Q/K/V triplet as one mathematically equivalent block-diagonal rank-96 adapter. All other modules remain rank 32. See `FUSION_PROVENANCE.json` for the conversion details.\nL83: Field  | Value\nL84: --- | ---\nL85: Internal recipe  | `sft-v4`\nL86: Training rows  | 494\nL87: Epochs  | 5\nL88: Learning rate  | `4.65e-4`\nL89: Maximum length  | 65,536\nL90: Release-tested reconstruction base revision  | `6a9e13bd6fc8f0983b9b99948120bc37f49c13e9`\nL91: ## Load without merging\nL92: \nL93:     `from peft import PeftModel\nL94:     from transformers import AutoModelForMultimodalLM\nL95: \nL96:     base = AutoModelForMultimodalLM.from_pretrained(\nL97:         \"Qwen/Qwen3.6-27B\",\nL98:         revision=\"6a9e13bd6fc8f0983b9b99948120bc37f49c13e9\",\nL99:         torch_dtype=\"auto\",\nL100:         device_map=\"auto\",\nL101:         token=True,\nL102:     )\nL103:     model = PeftModel.from_pretrained(base, \"Genghan/PTXBench-Qwen3.6-27B-s0\", token=True)\nL104:     `\nL105: Run `python merge_adapter.py` to create a standalone merged model directory. The merge requires the full base-model download and substantial CPU memory and disk space; it does not require a GPU.\nL106: \nL107: This checkpoint is intended for research on CUDA kernel generation and repair. It inherits the limitations of the base model and may emit incorrect or unsafe CUDA. Generated kernels must be compiled and evaluated in an isolated environment before use.\nL108: \nL109: Downloads last month\nL110:     5\nL111: \nL112: Inference Providers cite42†NEW L113: cite43†Image-Text-to-Text L114: \nL115: This model isn't deployed by any Inference Provider. cite44†🙋 Ask for provider support L116: ## Model tree for Genghan/PTXBench-Qwen3.6-27B-s0\nL117: \nL118: Base model\nL119: \nL120: cite45†Qwen/Qwen3.6-27B L121: \nL122: Finetuned\nL123: \nL124: (cite46†395 )\nL125: \nL126: this model\nL127: \nL128: ## Dataset used to train Genghan/PTXBench-Qwen3.6-27B-s0\nL129: \nL130: cite47†Genghan/PTXBenc